**Usage notes:**
++  need to be careful with mixins
    ++  the parentmost class with ``metaclass=CfgMeta`` must **always be the
        abstract config!** if you want to use mixin classes to define configs,
        you'll need to declare them as plain ``Protocol`` classes **without**
        the metaclass. (You can still use ``Secret`` and it will still be
        detected correctly!)
++  defining extra fields on a concrete config class is permissible
    ++  this can be useful if you're importing a library and want to add some
        additional config info to its namespace based on your particular
        use case for the library

**Dev notes:**
++  might want to relax the constraint forcing unique namespaces for concrete
    configs (maybe with a kwarg for strict vs non-strict). this would be **by
    far** the most pragmatic way of handling "okay but I want to have multiple
    abstract configs in the same namespace"; the alternative is a bunch of
    really messy mapping between abstract and config, and would require a
    major rewrite of the internal workings
    ++  one caveat here is that you'd need to be careful about whether or not
        to allow duplicate field names for separate configs on the same
        namespace
    ++  tbh though... namespaces are only meaningful if the backend decides
        they are. the better option here might just to write a custom backend
        that merges namespaces -- for example ``foo.bar`` and ``foo.baz`` both
        come from ``foo`` -- on an application-specific basis
    ++  **however, it might be smart to allow duplicate namespace=None classes.**
        not sure either way about this one. it would take some thought as well.



> Features ideas etc
    ++  ``get_active_cfg`` "namespace" kwarg
